{{define "denied.gohtml"}}{{template "layout" .}}{{end}}
{{define "content"}}
<div class="notice">
  <h1>This tool is for the arc42 maintainers</h1>
  <p class="lede">You are signed in as <strong>{{.Login}}</strong>. Editing training
    dates requires push access to <code>{{.Repo}}</code>, which only the two arc42
    maintainers have. Nothing is wrong with your account — there is simply nothing
    here for it to do.</p>

  <h2>Looking for the training dates?</h2>
  <p>Every upcoming arc42 training — dates, cities, languages and booking links —
    is on the public site. That is almost certainly what you came for.</p>
  <p><a class="button" href="https://trainings.arc42.org">Go to trainings.arc42.org</a></p>

  <h2>Are you a maintainer?</h2>
  <p>Then you are probably signed in with the wrong GitHub account — an easy thing
    to do when one browser is signed into several. Sign out, then sign in again
    with the account that has push access.</p>
  <form method="post" action="/auth/logout">
    <button class="secondary">Sign out of {{.Login}}</button>
  </form>

  <p class="hint">Access is checked against GitHub on every sign-in; this app keeps
    no user list of its own. Like the rest of arc42, it is open source — the code
    lives in <a href="https://github.com/{{.Repo}}">{{.Repo}}</a>.</p>
</div>
{{end}}
